    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ff243c16-a171-5388-9234-47ead08ae7b7",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $S$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(S)=- \\frac{5}{4}$\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} & - \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4} & 1 & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} & - \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4} & 1 & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2})|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{3}{2})|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} & - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{4} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2})(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{8}- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4})+(- \\frac{3}{2})(- \\frac{15}{16}+\\frac{15}{16})+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{8}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2})\\cdot (- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{8})+(- \\frac{3}{2})\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\cdot (- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}- \\frac{25}{16} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
