  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186059848,
      "id": "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93",
      "title": "Identifying Singular Matrices"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "89775eee-5b3a-59c0-8251-d2a6abc9248d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $P$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $P$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(P)=0$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{1}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{1}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ - \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+\\sqrt{3}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{5} & - \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{15}- \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{15})+\\frac{3}{5}(\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{8}{5})+\\sqrt{3}(- \\frac{12 \\sqrt{3}}{25}+\\frac{4 \\sqrt{3}}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\cdot (- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{5})+\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{11}{5}+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (- \\frac{8 \\sqrt{3}}{25}) \\\\  & =- \\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{33}{25}- \\frac{24}{25} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ea73f07d-ed1f-5ab5-a97c-10789c03a150",
