    "question": {
      ":question/id": "263540ee-8067-53d3-b96e-fcfd7730152e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $P$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $P$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(P)=- \\frac{3}{10} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{15}$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & - \\frac{1}{5} & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & - \\frac{1}{5} & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{5}|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2})|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{10})+\\frac{1}{5}(- \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})+(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{15}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{15}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{10})+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0+(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2})\\cdot (- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{15}) \\\\  & =- \\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
