    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "066edcff-aa57-5aad-b8ed-bf44751f3b3f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $S$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $S$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(S)=0$\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5})|\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{2}{5})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\end{aligned}|+(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3})|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & - \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5})(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5}- \\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{15})+(- \\frac{2}{5})(\\frac{4}{3}- \\frac{4}{3})+(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{25}+\\frac{6 \\sqrt{5}}{25}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5})\\cdot (- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3})+(- \\frac{2}{5})\\cdot 0+(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{3})\\cdot \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}- \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "61f800ca-bfa8-593e-84ff-d482810326cb",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
